<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Creticus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 54 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Metellus Creticus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Creticus was a Roman general and consul in 69 BCE. Sent against the Cretan cities, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> accused of aiding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>, he besieged Kydonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knossos">Knossos</a> and other towns between 69 and 67 BCE and conquered the whole island. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> then became a Roman province, later joined with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, with Gortyn as its capital, and he took the surname Creticus.</p></div>
